From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 7 Jun 2026 19:45:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00849/11171] [outer-loop] Phase 0 v1: whole-trace
 certification = base-rate (FORMAT MISMATCH, not verifier ability)

Verifier-as-self-improvement-reward de-risk. Whole-trace certification via the
production ensemble on 558 p01 traces (34% gold-correct): certified-correct set is
only 34-38% precise = ~base rate -> Phase-1 gate FAILS. BUT this is almost certainly
a FORMAT MISMATCH: Carnot's ensemble is a per-STEP process verifier (FoVer 0.91 AUROC
judges individual steps WITH problem context); fed whole-trace blobs with minimal rows
and no problem context it degenerates to base-rate -- exactly what we see. So this is
INCONCLUSIVE (likely mismatch), NOT a clean negative -- same v1->v2 pattern as #4.
Phase 0 v2 = per-step certification with problem context (score each reasoning_step in
context, certify trace iff no step flagged), needs proper FoVer-row data prep. Gate
the verifier-as-self-improvement-reward program on v2, not v1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
